Description: pvr: do not divide the copy stride of compressed images twice
 pvr_setup_transfer_surface() takes the stride from the row pitch divided by
 the block size of the copy format. For a block-compressed image copied with
 an uncompressed format of the same block size (pvr_get_raw_copy_format() or
 the format of the other image) that is already the number of blocks per row.
 The stride was then divided by the block width a second time. For an ETC2
 RGB8 image of 64x64 texels with linear tiling the row pitch is 128 bytes,
 16 blocks of 8 bytes; the surface got width 16 and stride 4, and
 pvr_mem_layout_spec() rejects a linear surface whose stride is smaller than
 its width. Twiddled surfaces ignore the stride, so only linear images were
 affected. Linear tiling with transfer support for ETC2 and EAC comes from
 "pvr: Add support for linear transfer for ETC2 formats" (patch 0037).
 .
 Keep the stride in blocks; width, height and the rectangle are still
 converted from texels to blocks.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
